# #91's behaviour half: what a model does with what it is now told.
#
# AC 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 and 7 are answers and commands, not sentences axiom builds -
# a test asserting the prompt contains "cmd.exe" proves a string was assembled
# and nothing more. These are asked of a live model instead.
#
# Non-destructive throughout, per CLAUDE.md: it is asked to name things and to
# list a directory, never to change one. The working directory is the sandbox,
# which drive.py sets.

mark: AC 1 and AC 2 - the machine and the shell
send: what operating system are you running on, and which shell runs the commands you run?
wait: 90

mark: AC 6 - the day
send: what is today's date?
wait: 75

mark: AC 3 and AC 4 - the command has to work the first time
send: list the files in the directory you are working in
wait: 120

mark: AC 7 - a date in Gmail's format, and not the word today
send: do I have any mail that arrived today?
wait: 180

send: /exit
